4 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127134 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127134 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "10169cf2-216d-5f27-afd2-083c26124615" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186127136 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186127137 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186127138 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186127139 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186127140 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127135 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0b31d3e4-9718-5bdd-98c1-263343513322" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127136 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127136 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127136 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "80e45dc4-fa69-5e93-8050-0585ec419222" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127137 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127137 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127137 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "8b63755c-73ea-518c-a235-eb0a7c358907" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127138 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127138 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127138 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b153270b-bae4-534c-b006-edf982a8418a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127139 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127139 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127139 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3b37e3ba-b5b1-555d-b35e-7155ecdab12e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127140 #edb/ref 1080 "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127140 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186127140 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4c1c58cc-cdb7-53d8-90da-a7e900572ef8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128938 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5490" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128938 #edb/ref 1071 "The vector $\\mathbf{v}$ and the matrix $A$ are given below. \nIf $\\mathbf{v}$ is an eigenvector of $A$ that corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda=3,$ then what is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$\n\n![](images/65/65004c0c3788085f6f11fcdf9b107c43004dd4f7f21c6b1ecd78b81a89c76f46.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128938 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "d6c73b7b-4981-5908-b694-be7f0e57b612" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128938 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -6 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-6{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & {R}_{1}:=\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -2 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-2){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Thus, $x_3$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain $x_2=x_3.$ From the first equation, we get $x_1=3x_3.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n![](images/a4/a4e3f32645ea033a5165c12ddb6a0563ae00f061e4e0f570ba739c531d28cd0b.svg)\n\nSetting, for instance, $x_3=1,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n![](images/b1/b1058a07d9ab58d8ec18ea08b8afb1e09e2dc97ae02f1289f730944fb075d370.svg)\n\nFinally, $\\dfrac{b}{c}=\\dfrac{1}{1}=1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128939 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5491" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128939 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an eigenvector of\n![](images/ac/acc39fa601e9dd28da49849b9e3e098441f7d9dc2b9ad9c1b58af9ae7e014d98.svg)\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $\\lambda=-2.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128939 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b087e601-c054-563c-b7ee-43e18c74ac51" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128939 #edb/ref 1074 "To compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =-2.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}]-(-2)[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors corresponding to this eigenvalue, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}3{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0 \\\\ {x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}↔{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $3$rd). Thus, $x_2$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain $x_3=0.$ Substituting this in the first equation, we get $x_1=-x_2.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n![](images/31/31ec85b3cd3afae1b23c4558b7e2d8d758f9aff3ed6fb02760684e2f25ccc948.svg)\n\nSetting, for instance, $x_2=1,$ we get the eigenvector\n![](images/1c/1c22d6fa620b2de744da62b5e05088a571cb74172cf4e031a87dd90f74adb00b.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128940 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5492" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128940 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/e9/e93ca6621010628ace0d692899b04fb981045bd570d6bb68a502a03ab02064ce.svg)\n\nThe vectors $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ are eigenvectors that correspond to the eigenvalues $\\lambda_1=1$ and $\\lambda_2=-1$ of the matrix $A,$ given above. Find the third eigenvector $\\mathbf{v}_3=\\big[ a, \\, b, \\, c \\big]^T$ such that the set $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_1,\\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3 \\}$ is linearly independent. What is the value of $\\dfrac{a}{c}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128940 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c22ab531-3377-5827-93d2-a13854b3308c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186128940 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $A$ is a diagonal matrix, we have that its eigenvalues are the entries in the main diagonal, that is, $\\lambda_1=1,$ $\\lambda_2=-1$ and $\\lambda_3=4.$ \n\nAlso, since we obtained three distinct eigenvalues, the set of eigenvectors $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_1,\\mathbf{v}_2, \\mathbf{v}_3 \\},$ where each vector corresponds to different eigenvalue, will be linearly independent.\n\nNow, recall that $\\mathbf{v}_1$ and $\\mathbf{v}_2$ correspond to the eigenvalues $\\lambda_1=1$ and $\\lambda_2=-1.$ Thus, the third eigenvector $\\mathbf{v}_3$ must correspond to $\\lambda_3=4.$ \n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =4.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]-4[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors corresponding to this eigenvalue, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{1}=0 \\\\ -5{x}_{2}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the augmented matrix $M$ is already in its row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this matrix, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Thus, $x_3$ is a free variable. From the first and second equations, we obtain $x_1=x_2=0.$  Therefore, the general solution is\n![](images/4b/4be28d6335835749df1f44a49e8cbe52eaceb3f2efbaccf6a085caa08d6d60ac.svg)\n\nSetting, for instance, $x_3=1,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n![](images/f7/f70927c82679024a0d9b58a2d30bb404968cac08bf2dca98f7e247742dad6f33.svg)\n\nFinally, $\\dfrac{a}{c}=\\dfrac{0}{1}=0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186048775 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129602 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323848 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323866 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323907 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323912 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating the Components of an Eigenvector Corresponding to a Given Eigenvalue" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128938 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129127 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "c2c79885-7848-51e3-9f96-6a109e776fd5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272147 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323915 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186357395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186382052 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186395838 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399187 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399194 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186399241 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186431011 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1039 "Calculating an Eigenvector Corresponding to a Given Eigenvalue" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186128939 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129128 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "4def2d61-0093-53cf-bcbb-1d2c3e6e1738" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129603 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129607 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186272149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323867 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129129 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186323913 #edb/ref 17592186045417] 