#edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129608 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b92ae563-4565-5947-89cb-f058a9c4a4a5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129609 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186127135 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129609 #edb/ref 1069 "q-37405" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129609 #edb/ref 1071 "Find an eigenvector of $A = \\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$\nthat corresponds to the eigenvalue $λ =-1$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129609 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "21a6142d-2e2d-5db8-9f67-5431e9644165" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129964 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1061 20099 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "875dc5aa-e4f4-50f8-a30e-d5ed46d77e32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129963 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130347 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129965 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1061 20100 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "59537f37-7060-5544-9b4a-84501e450c50" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129964 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129127 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130084 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1061 20101 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8a926ac2-afd2-5b57-8911-c3b8dac86d39" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129965 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129128 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129966 #edb/ref 1061 20102 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129966 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5d1fcdf4-d676-5ff5-bf31-d7e371f43f08" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129966 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129129 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186129966 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1061 27265 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "3314b023-f15c-5f8b-a4e4-aeea702377a2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130084 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1064 "Consider the following $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n![](images/4f/4fd591d8028847aa7e1d11e840acdb192703d152f9c397e40fec98fd1e281c41.svg)\n\nIf we are told that one of the eigenvalues of this matrix is $\\lambda = 3,$ how do we calculate the corresponding eigenvector?\n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation\n\n$$\n(A - \\lambda I) \\textbf{x}=\\mathbf{0}.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =3.$ So, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -4\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -8 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, to find the eigenvectors, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}6{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -3{x}_{2}+6{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 3{x}_{2}-7{x}_{3}=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we row-reduce the augmented matrix $M$ to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+\\frac{1}{2}{R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-\\frac{1}{2}){R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -3 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+\\frac{3}{2}{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & 6 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn this reduced matrix, there are two pivot columns (the $2$nd and $3$rd). Thus, $x_1$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we have $x_3 = 0.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we obtain $x_2 = 0.$ Therefore, the general solution is\n\n![](images/70/705dd92c7330897f35671b66866791160b9d7f65e3280d5ccb9d992405c08942.svg)\n\nSetting $x_1=1,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n![](images/2a/2a5dd6c35fb81134f13e765e0a02be4ea2feedfd878a1923491813492739ef00.svg)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1065 3566 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "b1a9d148-15f7-5878-8f36-f19ee99c49d6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130347 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1064 "Note the following important theorem.\n\n*The set of eigenvectors $\\{ \\mathbf{v}_1,\\mathbf{v}_2, \\ldots, \\mathbf{v}_k \\}$ of a matrix $A,$ where each vector $\\mathbf v_i$ corresponds to a different eigenvalue, is linearly independent.*\n\n**Watch out!** Eigenvectors that correspond to the *same* eigenvalue *can* be (and very often *will* be) linearly dependent." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1065 4432 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "c0f0f6d3-c9e1-52a6-bf51-244bb7751a9d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130403 #edb/ref 1067 "Eigenvectors That Correspond to Different Eigenvalues" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269719 #edb/ref 1080 "-5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269719 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186269719 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "31dcee0a-b3fd-57c4-97a4-a11665baed4f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270414 #edb/ref 1080 "-7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270414 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270414 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "84c9b455-f22d-5907-ad80-413eec64e049" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270431 #edb/ref 1080 "7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270431 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270431 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "85eb0455-8d8c-5fc3-86b6-d1a10c4afe7c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270905 #edb/ref 1080 "5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270905 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186270905 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "b9539882-4d96-5e96-8872-29f5b35c6107" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271215 #edb/ref 1080 "3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271215 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271215 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ddb05c8c-f619-5174-8242-5d23cb7c21f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186269719 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270414 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186270905 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186271215 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186270431 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186271869 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c58f795f-dc1c-59c4-9499-e84bc1457919" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272149 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186271869 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272149 #edb/ref 1069 "q-140720" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272149 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272149 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe vectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ are eigenvectors that correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ of the matrix $A,$ given above. Find the third eigenvector ${v}_{3}=[a,\\,b,\\,c]^{T}$ such that the set $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\}$ is linearly independent. What is the value of $\\frac{a}{b}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272149 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f3c0726d-3efe-576b-8418-4bde00e5fffc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186272149 #edb/ref 1074 "Since $A$ is an upper triangular matrix, we have that its eigenvalues are the entries in the main diagonal, that is, ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$ \n\nAlso, since we obtained three distinct eigenvalues, the set of eigenvectors $\\{{v}_{1},{v}_{2},{v}_{3}\\},$ where each vector corresponds to different eigenvalue, will be linearly independent.\n\nNow, recall that ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}$ correspond to the eigenvalues ${\\lambda }_{1}=2$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}=-3.$ Thus, the third eigenvector ${v}_{3}$ must correspond to ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$ \n\nTo compute the eigenvectors of a matrix, we need to find non-zero solutions of the matrix equation \n\n$$\n(A-\\lambda I)\\text{x}=0.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn our case, we have $\\lambda =1.$ So, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-\\lambda I & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]-1[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the eigenvectors corresponding to this eigenvalue, we have to solve the corresponding homogeneous system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -4{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 0=0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the augmented matrix $M$ is already in its row echelon form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn the reduced matrix above, there are two pivot columns (the $1$st and the $2$nd). Thus, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable. From the second equation, we obtain ${x}_{2}=\\frac{1}{4}{x}_{3}.$ Substituting this into the first equation, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}{x}_{3}+2{x}_{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{4}{x}_{3} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nSetting, for instance, ${x}_{3}=4,$ we get the following eigenvector:\n\n$$\nv=[\\begin{aligned}a \\\\ b \\\\ c\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFinally, $\\frac{a}{b}=\\frac{7}{1}=7.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321165 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 12\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321165 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321165 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "01cac26b-e387-5346-8ee2-695230b9e26f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321225 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{3}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321225 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321225 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "0a29aa16-6c63-5a61-91a9-1f74b2ed3f26" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321305 #edb/ref 1080 "2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321305 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321305 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "139de0b1-a7cc-5a6f-8d11-174a489bfe2c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321448 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321448 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321448 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "26853257-a15d-56bd-baf3-05cb4af2b356" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321596 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{2}{3}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321596 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321596 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "3a995098-985b-5a0d-8363-a15a9776bdf5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321914 #edb/ref 1080 "4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321914 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186321914 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6215dc3a-949b-5a88-b400-1754de3451a6" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322046 #edb/ref 1080 "[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322046 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186322046 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "728e1505-0be2-5108-b4fa-9ed5d07278e7" #edb/ref 175